 details given of the specifics of the charges about what happened in Vietnam.  [Former Kerry crewmate Patrick RUNYON&#134;- recalls that night; says the investigator added things to his statement.]  [\"Unfit for Command\" co-author John O'NEILL&#134;- recounts Kerry shooting a young Viet Cong sniper in the back.]  Statement from \"Chicago Tribune\" editor William Rood&#134;&#134; in response quoted.  [Former Swift boat officer Jim RUSSELL&#134;- asserts there was enemy fire that day.]", "segment_duration": 270, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 762816, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "8XTBUE78uK", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 762815, "segment_id": "G553ty3PuO", "segment_broadcast_id": "8XTBUE78uK", "segment_title": "Iraq / Al-Sadr Revolt / Najaf", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Report introduced. \n (Pentagon: Martha Raddatz)  The ongoing siege in Najaf, Iraq, featured; scenes shown of US warplanes firing on militant targets, of American troops on the ground firing on the forces of Shiite cleric Muqtada al-Sadr & of armed insurgents; details given of the deliberate nature of the standoff.  [1st Cavalry Div. Sgt. Danny GIFFORD&#134;, Capt. Jason TOEPFER&#134;- talk about the fighting.]  [Reporter Stephanie GOSK&#134;- comments on the battle.]", "segment_duration": 110, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 762817, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast